---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout 
  title="Edge Agents & Closed Networks" 
  description="Connect isolated VPCs, private clouds, and on-premises subnets to duckJump using outbound TLS reverse tunnels."
  currentSlug="edge-agents"
>
  <div class="space-y-8">
    
    <div>
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-2.5 py-1 rounded bg-teal-500/10 text-teal-400 border border-teal-500/20 text-xs font-mono mb-3">
        Hybrid Cloud & Zero-Trust
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-white tracking-tight">
        Edge Sites & Reverse Tunnels
      </h1>
      <p class="text-slate-400 text-lg mt-2 leading-relaxed">
        Reach internal hosts in closed networks, private AWS/GCP VPCs, or branch offices without opening inbound firewall ports, VPN tunnels, or port forwarding.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- How Edge Agent Works -->
    <div class="space-y-4 pt-4 border-t border-slate-800">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">1. Outbound Multiplexed Tunnels</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        The lightweight <code class="text-amber-300">duckjump-agent</code> binary runs inside the target network. It initiates an outbound TLS connection over WebSockets (WSS) to the central gateway and multiplexes multiple sessions using yamux:
      </p>

      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-slate-950 border border-slate-800 font-mono text-xs text-slate-300 overflow-x-auto space-y-2">
        <pre class="text-slate-300">
Closed Private Network (VPC / On-Prem)              Public / Bastion DMZ
┌───────────────────────────────────────┐            ┌─────────────────────────────┐
│ Target Hosts (SSH, Windows RDP, VNC)  │            │ duckjump-gw (Gateway)       │
│                ▲                      │            │                             │
│                │ LAN traffic          │            │                             │
│ ┌───────────────────────────────────┐ │            │                             │
│ │ duckjump-agent                    │ ├──WSS+yamux─▶ Edge Agent Hub              │
│ │ /etc/duckjump-agent/token         │ │ (Outbound) │                             │
│ └───────────────────────────────────┘ │            └─────────────────────────────┘
└───────────────────────────────────────┘
        </pre>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Agent Setup -->
    <div class="space-y-4 pt-4 border-t border-slate-800">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">2. Setting Up an Edge Site</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        Setting up an edge site is automated directly from the duckJump web console:
      </p>

      <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 text-sm text-slate-300 space-y-3">
        <li>In the duckJump UI, navigate to <strong class="text-white">Sites → New Site</strong>. Select <strong class="text-sky-400">Edge agent (closed network)</strong> and enter a name (e.g. <code class="text-amber-300">branch-office-1</code>).</li>
        <li>Configure your permitted subnets and ports in the modal (e.g. <code class="text-emerald-400">0.0.0.0/0:22,3389,5900</code> or <code class="text-emerald-400">10.10.0.0/24:22,3389</code>).</li>
        <li>Copy and run the generated one-liner command on the target Linux machine inside the private network:</li>
      </ol>

      <div class="bg-slate-950 p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-800 font-mono text-xs text-slate-300 space-y-2">
        <div class="text-slate-500"># Automated installation as a managed systemd service:</div>
        <div class="text-sky-300">curl -fsSL "https://bastion.example.com:8090/agent/install.sh?token=&lt;TOKEN&gt;&allow=0.0.0.0/0:22,3389,5900" | sudo bash</div>
      </div>

      <p class="text-slate-400 text-xs leading-relaxed">
        The installer downloads the agent binary to <code class="text-white">/usr/local/bin/duckjump-agent</code>, saves the token to <code class="text-white">/etc/duckjump-agent/token</code> (mode 0600), writes configuration to <code class="text-white">/etc/duckjump-agent/agent.env</code>, and enables/starts the <code class="text-white">duckjump-agent.service</code> systemd unit with full privilege drop (<code class="text-white">DynamicUser=yes</code>).
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Local Allow-Lists -->
    <div class="space-y-4 pt-4 border-t border-slate-800">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">3. Enforced Local Allow-Lists (-allow)</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        To adhere to strict Zero-Trust isolation, the agent enforces a local allow list (<code class="text-amber-300">DUCKJUMP_AGENT_ALLOW</code> or flag <code class="text-amber-300">-allow</code>). The agent parses every dial request sent by the bastion and rejects any target IP address or port not explicitly listed in its local rules:
      </p>

      <div class="bg-slate-950 p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-800 font-mono text-xs text-slate-300 space-y-1">
        <div class="text-slate-500"># /etc/duckjump-agent/agent.env</div>
        <div>DUCKJUMP_AGENT_SERVER="wss://bastion.example.com:8090/agent/connect"</div>
        <div class="text-amber-300">DUCKJUMP_AGENT_ALLOW="10.10.0.0/24:22,3389 192.168.1.0/24:22,3389,5900"</div>
      </div>

      <p class="text-slate-400 text-xs">
        Format: <code class="text-white">CIDR[:port,port...]</code> separated by spaces. An empty allow list refuses all dials.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Lifecycle and HA -->
    <div class="space-y-4 pt-4 border-t border-slate-800">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">4. Lifecycle & Redundancy</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-sm text-slate-300 space-y-2">
        <li><strong>Graceful Shutdown:</strong> When the agent is stopped (<code class="text-white">sudo systemctl stop duckjump-agent</code>), the gateway immediately detects the closed session, removes the agent from the active pool, and aborts pending tickets.</li>
        <li><strong>Redundancy:</strong> Multiple agent instances can be run within the same network pointing to the same site token. Traffic across active sessions is automatically load-balanced across live agents.</li>
        <li><strong>Auto-Reconnect:</strong> If network connectivity drops or the gateway restarts, the agent reconnects with exponential backoff.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

  </div>
</DocsLayout>
